# Practical 5: Infinite Scroll with TanStack Query
---

## What I Did

In this practical I implemented infinite scrolling in the TikTok clone's video feed using TanStack Query and cursor-based pagination. Previously the feed made a single API request and returned every video in the database at once. Now it loads 5 videos at a time and automatically fetches the next batch as the user scrolls toward the bottom — exactly like the real TikTok feed.

---

## Tech Stack Added

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `@tanstack/react-query` | Data fetching, caching, and infinite scroll state management |
| `@tanstack/react-query-devtools` | Debug panel showing query state in browser |
| Intersection Observer API | Detects when user scrolls to bottom to trigger next page load |
| Cursor-based pagination | Efficient database querying without offset drift |

---

## What Changed

### Backend
- Updated `getAllVideos` in `videoController.js` — now accepts `cursor` and `limit` query params
- Updated `getFollowingVideos` — same cursor-based pagination added
- Response format changed from plain array to:
  ```json
  { "videos": [...], "nextCursor": 42, "hasNextPage": true }
  ```

### Frontend
- Updated `src/app/layout.js` — added `QueryClientProvider` wrapping the whole app
- Updated `src/services/videoService.js` — `getAllVideos` and `getFollowingVideos` now accept cursor param
- Created `src/hooks/useIntersectionObserver.js` — reusable hook for detecting scroll position
- Updated `src/components/ui/VideoFeed.jsx` — replaced `useState/useEffect` fetch with `useInfiniteQuery`
- Updated `src/app/page.js` and `src/app/following/page.jsx` — pass `userInteracted` down to feed
- Fixed `src/app/explore/page.jsx` — updated to handle new paginated response format

